<!-- Fabricated System B application (bussard's own work, MIT; no vendor data)
     for the activity of a <choose> (issues #563 and #474).

     #563: ETS decides activity per ParameterRef. "Changeover" (P-1) is shown
     through R-1; a <choose> on its second ref R-2 (Access="Read", never
     shown) selects no branch, so object 2 and "Cycle" (P-3) stay out. The
     one-member union holds "Mode" (UP-1), shown through R-4; its ref R-5
     is shown only when "Selector" (P-5) is 0 (it is 1), so a <choose> on R-5
     selects no branch either, although R-5 reads the live shared memory:
     object 3 and "Offset" (P-6) stay out.

     #474: a <choose> on a never-shown parameter without memory takes its
     default branch, as ETS does. "AlwaysFalse" (P-7, a checkbox with
     Access="Read" and Value 0, the Zennio Flat construct) reaches object 4 and
     "Dummy" (P-8); object 4 has every flag disabled, so the group-object table
     leaves it out, as ETS does with the Flat "dummy" objects. "Input A" (P-9,
     TypeNone, Access="None", empty Value, the ABB construct) steers a whole
     channel: object 5. "Variant" (P-10, Access="None", Value 1) steers by a
     matching test: object 6. "Device active" (P-11, Access="Read", Value 1,
     the ABB Modbus gateway construct) has a "0" branch beside its default
     one, and the default is taken: object 7. "General" (P-12, Value 0, the
     ABB 0701 R_Allgemein construct) takes its only, default branch: object 8.
     -->
